application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Local evidence (2026-11-09 PST, ubuntu:26.04 container on colima, bwrap 0.11.1, privileged root container). Before the fix at 872e7f6c3fd: the gate fails head/gates with EBUSY then EEXIST on .mutation-pytest, matching the CI artifact. With the committed fix (_bwrap_argv binds only outermost allow-list paths): the real gate, run per shard under bwrap, passes signing, next-batch, gates, validate, compact-policy and push-policy, with no UNSANDBOXED waiver line in any shard's stderr. reducer-processors fails its clean baseline on test_cache_invalidated_on_file_deletion (equal mtime), which fails 16/30 in the same container with no sandbox; tracked in fast-knotty-xiaosaurus. New live test test_the_child_can_delete_and_recreate_a_nested_basetemp fails under real bwrap before the fix (rmtree EBUSY) and passes after; full test_mutation_sandbox.py passes 47/47 under REBAR_REQUIRE_SANDBOX_ENFORCEMENT=1 in the container. Fail-open waiver filed separately as nonfat-wimpy-aurochs (a different cause: the workflow's unconditional REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED).","timestamp":1794265806484172001}],"created_at":1794262069558678001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a6fb7588-813f-4c9e-8de3-887d07bd0202","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c0a9-e8d2-8058-4250"}],"description":"## Observation\n- Gerrit change 3335 (Release 0.15.0, a version-only change) got Verified -1 on 2026-11-09 at 14:00 PST. Run 42702801672: all 7 `bounded mutation gate` shards fail with `baseline-test: head/<shard>: selected clean tests failed`. Every pytest, lint, typecheck, artifact-probe and optionality job passed.\n- The shard artifact `head-clean.txt` (gates shard) shows the clean baseline erroring on its first test: pytest's rm_rf of `--basetemp` fails with `OSError: [Errno 16] Device or resource busy: '/tmp/rebar-mutation-*/gates-head/.mutation-pytest'`, then `tmp_path_factory.mktemp` raises `FileExistsError: [Errno 17]` on the same path (tests/conftest.py:609). No mutant ran.\n- Working comparison: run 41939410124 (change 3328, 2026-11-04 16:11 PST) passed all 7 shards on runner image ubuntu-24.04. Its shard logs show `bwrap is installed but cannot create a namespace (bwrap: setting up uid map: Permission denied)` and `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED is set: running mutation tests UNSANDBOXED`, so the gate ran unsandboxed. Run 42702801672 ran on ubuntu-26.04, where bwrap 0.11.1 creates the namespace and the waiver line is absent, so the sandboxed path executed in CI for the first time.\n\n## Reproduction (2026-11-09 PST, ubuntu:26.04 container under colima, bwrap 0.11.1, run as root in a privileged container because the colima VM's AppArmor denies the non-root uid map)\n- Minimal: inside `bwrap --ro-bind / / --dev /dev --proc /proc --bind ROOT ROOT --bind ROOT/.mutation-pytest ROOT/.mutation-pytest`, `shutil.rmtree(ROOT/.mutation-pytest)` raises `[Errno 16] Device or resource busy` and the following `os.mkdir` raises `[Errno 17] File exists`. With only `--bind ROOT ROOT`, the same rmtree + mkdir succeeds.\n- Real gate: `scripts/mutation_gate.py run --shard gates` at 872e7f6c3fd fails `baseline-test: head/gates`, and `head-clean.txt` carries the same EBUSY then EEXIST on `.mutation-pytest` as the CI artifact.\n- Experiment: the same tree with the gate's allow-list reduced to `(root,)` runs the `signing` shard's clean baseline (39 passed) and `mutmut run` to completion under bwrap, so the EBUSY/EEXIST is gone. The `reducer-processors` clean baseline then failed on `test_cache_invalidated_on_file_deletion` (equal mtime). That test fails 16 of 30 runs in the same container with no sandbox at all, so it is a host timestamp-granularity flake independent of the sandbox, tracked in `fast-knotty-xiaosaurus`; it passes on GitHub's hosted runners. The other 5 shards (`next-batch`, `gates`, `validate`, `compact-policy`, `push-policy`) passed the gate end to end under bwrap with that change, so 6 of 7 shards pass sandboxed and the seventh is blocked only by the unrelated flake.\n\n## Root cause\n`execute_shard` and `_diagnose_non_killed` (scripts/mutation_gate.py) pass `allow=(root, basetemp)` with `basetemp = root / \".mutation-pytest\"`, a path nested inside `root`. `_bwrap_argv` (scripts/mutation_sandbox.py) emits one `--bind` per entry, so inside the namespace `.mutation-pytest` is a separate mount point stacked on an already-writable bind. The kernel refuses to remove or rename a mount point (EBUSY), and pytest's `--basetemp` setup always deletes and recreates that directory. The nested bind adds no write permission, because `root` is already writable. The defect has existed since the sandbox landed (a26a73277c8, 2026-08-26) and stayed hidden because CI's bwrap never started until the runner image moved to ubuntu-26.04.\n\n## Approach\nFix it in `_bwrap_argv`, where the mount layout is decided, so every caller is covered: bind only the outermost existing allow-list paths and drop any entry already inside another bound entry. Nesting is decided with `Path.parents` on resolved paths, not string prefixes, so `/a/b` does not swallow `/a/bc`. Missing entries are dropped (with the existing warning) before nesting is decided, so a nested entry whose parent is missing is still bound. The writable set is unchanged: everything a dropped entry covered is writable through its ancestor, and nothing new becomes writable, so the sandbox is not weakened. The gate keeps its `(root, basetemp)` contract and the Seatbelt path is unchanged (subpath rules have no mount points). No new config key, env var or feature flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py`: `_bwrap_argv` collapses nested allow-list entries; docstring states why.\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py`: a `@live` test that runs a child under `wrap(allow=(root, basetemp))` which deletes and recreates the nested basetemp (pytest's own sequence), then proves a write outside the allow-list is still denied; platform-independent argv tests for nested, sibling, prefix-sharing (`/a/b` vs `/a/bc`) and missing-parent entries.\n- `.github/mutation-shards.toml`: add `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py` to `global_support`. Today it is absent, so a change to the module that wraps every shard's test run selects no shard and the gate never exercises it; this change would itself select zero shards and could not meet the second criterion.\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py`: assert `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py` is in `global_support`, alongside the existing `scripts/mutation_gate.py` assertion.\n- The fail-open waiver in `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` is a different cause and is tracked separately in `nonfat-wimpy-aurochs`.\n\n## Testing\n- New `@live` test fails before the fix under real bwrap (EBUSY) and passes after; it also runs on macOS under Seatbelt and in CI's `sandbox enforcement (Linux bwrap, gating)` lane, which sets `REBAR_REQUIRE_SANDBOX_ENFORCEMENT=1` so it cannot skip there.\n- Argv unit tests run on every lane without a sandbox.\n- Re-run the real gate on all 7 shards in the ubuntu:26.04 container with the fix.\n- `make verify` before pushing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The mutation gate's clean baseline passes under a working bwrap sandbox, for example by binding a parent directory writable and passing pytest a basetemp beneath it, with a test that runs the bwrap argv shape against a bind-mounted basetemp.\n- [ ] `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py` is listed in `global_support` in `.github/mutation-shards.toml`, so a change to it selects every shard, and `tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py` asserts that membership.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A Verified run on ubuntu-26.04 that selects all 7 shards passes them.\n      provenance: environment=GitHub Actions navapbc/rebar ubuntu-26.04 runners; principal=CI GITHUB_TOKEN; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read from the Verified run's mutation shard conclusions","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"bind only outermost allow-list paths so nested basetemp is not a mount point"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"live test deleting and recreating a nested basetemp under the sandbox; argv nesting unit tests"},{"path":".github/mutation-shards.toml","reason":"add scripts/mutation_sandbox.py to global_support so sandbox changes select every shard"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py","reason":"assert mutation_sandbox.py is a global_support path"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5879541d-6b45-42fc-a124-f3560a2fd61f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f86a-c0ce-f107-405f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Mutation gate fails every shard on ubuntu-26.04: bwrap bind-mounts pytest basetemp, so clean baseline hits EBUSY/EEXIST","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["db7ab619-ad27-4bc7-b94b-6c25f71feb5b","a6fb7588-813f-4c9e-8de3-887d07bd0202","93e5f145-ce0d-495c-9e32-697cb4024d96","ef2691a8-7191-40ab-8318-96d4d51ea669","ebfa8f4b-b007-4231-ad00-79607e7a4582","5879541d-6b45-42fc-a124-f3560a2fd61f","386b915e-a27b-4aac-be24-03894cc52906","cf35d311-9497-447e-bdd2-4617642784d7","25574f7e-3a65-4935-889e-9ca964b2c3cc","280e4051-f87f-46a4-8bda-bb111ae6a1e7"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794265806484172002,"uuid":"51e69203-0a0e-4398-aa40-d7aab8a3e3d4"}